# Same turns as the Blood-token scenario, but Bombardiers sacrifices the Bloodtithe Harvester (mana value 2) for 2 + 2 = 4
# damage, and Bot2 responds by Lightning Bolting the Bombardiers. The ability is already on the stack, so it resolves
# without its source: it still deals 4 to Bot2, which was counted from the mana value the Harvester had as it was
# sacrificed (CR 608.2h, last-known information) - and the Bombardiers dealt no combat damage.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mountain
Bloodtithe Harvester
Broadside Bombardiers
Mountain
Mountain x3
Mountain x6

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bloodtithe Harvester.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Broadside Bombardiers.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Broadside Bombardiers > Bot2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Broadside Bombardiers.Activate(Bot2)
Bot1.Choose(Bloodtithe Harvester)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Broadside Bombardiers)
Bot1.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot1.Graveyard = Broadside Bombardiers; Bloodtithe Harvester
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Island
